{
  "_readme": "Parametric cartridge/ammo builder data (rifle-ammo-store plan, S1). Replaces catalog.data.json's enumerated rifles/loads with per-cartridge curve parameters + slider bands that game/ballistic-derivation.ts (S2) turns into MV/BC/length/recoil/Sg on demand, and game/spec.ts + catalog.ts's resolve*ForSpec (S3) turn into player-facing RifleModel/AmmoLoad shapes. Nothing in the app reads this file yet (S1 is data + consistency tests only).",
  "_provenance": "Design/Plans/rifle-ammo-store-plan.md §3, itself drawn from Design/bullet-catalog/build-data-reference.md §2-3 (validated against Litz Appendix A + Hornady 10th ed. + research runs R1-R3). Per-cartridge a/k/bands/platform rows are transcribed verbatim from plan §3.1-3.4 — not re-derived. `presets` are compiled per plan S1 step 3 (D18): the 8 shipped catalog.data.json loads (22lr/223/65cm/308 x match/bulk) plus the 2 oracle-only loads (338lm, 50bmg) from GameBuild/validation/loads.json. Preset i7 for 223/65cm/308 is taken verbatim from plan §2.2's implied-i7 column; i7 for the two oracle-only presets (338lm-300-match, 50bmg-661-m33) is computed here from the oracle's own box SD/BC7 (not given directly in the plan) — both land inside their cartridge's i7 band and the global 0.811-1.437 plausibility screen. .22 LR presets are handled per D8 (G1, authored BC, no i7): trueBc/lengthMOverride for 22lr-match are aligned to the golden-vector oracle (22lr-40-standard) rather than the older, non-oracle-matching catalog.data.json value of 0.134, on the same D9 logic that already forces oracle-pinned length overrides; 22lr-bulk needs an mvFpsOverride because the weight-driven curve has no way to distinguish two products at the identical 40 gr weight. NOTE ON mvFpsOverride SEMANTICS (resolved at S3, not S1): the velocity curve reproduces the §2.2 table's 'box MV' column, i.e. BELIEVED (advertised) muzzle velocity, not true — confirmed by cross-checking the .223/65cm/308 anchor rows against catalog.data.json's boxMvMps, all of which match the believed figure, not trueBaseMvMps. So every mvFpsOverride in this file (including .223 bulk's 3250) stands in for the derived BELIEVED MV; game/spec.ts (S3) computes trueBaseMv = believedMv / (1 + grades[grade].mvOptimism), inverting D10's stated formula. 22lr-bulk's override is therefore catalog.data.json's old BELIEVED boxMvMps (1070 fps), not its trueBaseMvMps (1055 fps, an earlier draft of this file had this backwards and was corrected before S3 consumed it). NOTED DISCREPANCY (not corrected, logged per plan §1b spirit): the plan's own 338lm anchor (300 gr @ 2720 fps) is 5 fps below the golden-vector oracle's box figure for the same load (2725 fps, GameBuild/validation/loads.json '338lm-300-match') — used as given ('do not re-derive'); the resulting ~0.2% preset MV gap does not affect the engine golden-vector harness, which diffs the physics engine against BallisticsToolkit directly and never reads this file.",
  "_units": "Cartridge/slider/platform fields are authored in their NATIVE units exactly as tabulated in the plan (weight: grains, barrel/length: inches, velocity curve: fps, i7: dimensionless, capacity: gr H2O) — ballistic-derivation.ts (S2) converts to SI via units/ at compute time, per execution-protocol §4.4 (no inline unit math). Fields that bypass the derivation formulas entirely (grade hidden-truth ranges consumed by hidden-truth.ts; preset lengthMOverride, which stands in for the L=C*SD derivation on oracle-pinned presets) are authored directly in SI (m/s, m) to stay bit-exact with GameBuild/validation/loads.json's own si block. preset mvFpsOverride is in fps (native), matching the box figures it stands in for.",
  "catalogVersion": 2,
